{%- comment -%}
  fye-buybox-centre — the centre-diamond chooser, for semi-mount rings.

  Rendered by main-product AFTER fye-buybox-eternity, not instead of it. An
  engagement ring's buy box is the ordinary Metal x Diamond Quality one; this
  is an extra panel on top of it, and MOST ENGAGEMENT RINGS DO NOT GET IT.
  Ed, 31/08/2026.

  ── THE GATE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  All three metafields, or no panel — Ed's ruling, 31/08/2026:

      fye.centre_shape   "Round"
      fye.carat_min      0.8
      fye.carat_max      1.3

  plus the section's `enable_centre_diamond`, which product.complete.json,
  product.gemset.json, product.gents.json and product.plain.json untick.

  The `-SMT` SKU tail is NOT the gate, though the two agree in practice: 30 of
  30 sampled -smt products carry all three metafields. A SKU convention is a
  naming habit; a metafield is data someone entered on purpose.

  ── NOTHING IS SELECTED ON LOAD ───────────────────────────────────────────

  Ed, 31/08/2026. No mode card carries `is-on`, every mode body is hidden, and
  no stone is implied. Live preselects "Required", which quietly makes the
  most expensive route the default and means a shopper can reach the basket
  without ever having made the decision.

  The consequence is a hard requirement on fye-ui.js: ADD TO CART MUST BE
  BLOCKED until a mode is chosen. An unselected chooser is not a neutral
  state — it is an incomplete order.

  Each card carries a real radio mark (`.pdp__radio`) — Ed, 31/08/2026: it is
  the signpost that says "pick one of these". The cards are `role="radio"`
  inside a `role="radiogroup"`, so the mark is decorative and hidden from
  assistive tech, which reads the state off aria-checked instead.

  ── THE THREE MODES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    required  the ring plus a stone we supply. The stone is its OWN cart line,
              chosen in the picker modal.
    supplied  the customer sends their own stone. Adds the centre-diamond
              setting fee as its own line, and requires a ticked waiver.
    none      semi-mount only. Nothing added, price as shown.

  Copy is kept to a few words per card because the three sit side by side —
  Ed, 31/08/2026. A card ~200px wide cannot hold a sentence without wrapping
  to four lines and dragging the panel down the page.

  ── PROPERTY NAMES ARE A CONTRACT ─────────────────────────────────────────

  Verbatim from live — the workshop reads these off orders, so a "tidier"
  spelling here is a production error:

      "Centre Diamond"   "Customer's own diamond" | "Semi-mount only"
      "Setting service"
      "Waiver"

  Every add-on line also carries "For ring" and "Ring SKU" so the cart can
  group them; those are set by fye-ui.js at add time, not here, because the
  SKU depends on the variant chosen.

  ── WHAT THIS SNIPPET DOES NOT DO ─────────────────────────────────────────

  It renders the modal SHELL and the mode cards. The stones themselves are
  fetched at runtime from templates/collection.cdc-json.liquid and injected by
  fye-ui.js — there is no server-rendered stone list, because the feed is
  15,000+ products and the carat window is per ring.

  Parameters: product, settings (the section's)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = settings
  assign p = product
  assign mf = p.metafields.fye

  assign shape = mf.centre_shape
  assign ct_min = mf.carat_min
  assign ct_max = mf.carat_max

  comment
    "a Round" but "an Emerald". Live builds the same sentence; the article is
    chosen from the first letter rather than a lookup table so a shape added
    to the catalogue tomorrow reads correctly without a code change.
  endcomment
  assign article = 'a'
  assign first_letter = shape | slice: 0, 1 | downcase
  assign vowels = 'a,e,i,o,u' | split: ','
  if vowels contains first_letter
    assign article = 'an'
  endif

  assign shape_lower = shape | downcase

  comment
    The suitability sentence. Built from the metafields, because a note typed
    into a section setting cannot know the shape of the ring it is shown on.
    custom.centre_suitability overrides per product; the section setting is
    the last resort.
  endcomment
  assign suitability = 'This ring is suitable for ' | append: article | append: ' ' | append: shape | append: ' cut centre diamond, ' | append: ct_min | append: '–' | append: ct_max | append: 'ct.'
  if p.metafields.custom.centre_suitability != blank
    assign suitability = p.metafields.custom.centre_suitability
  endif

  comment
    The fee price setting is only the ON-PAGE PREVIEW; the money charged comes
    from the fee product's own price when its line is added. So a missing
    figure suppresses the "+£x" line and nothing else.
  endcomment
  assign show_centre_fee_price = false
  if s.centre_fee_price_pennies > 0
    assign show_centre_fee_price = true
  endif

  comment
    Shape sub-collection handles, for the "see them all" link and for the
    feed. Note the asymmetry live uses: "natural" but "lab-grown".
  endcomment
  assign shape_slug = shape | downcase | replace: ' ', '-'
  assign natural_handle = shape_slug | append: '-natural-diamonds'
  assign lab_handle = shape_slug | append: '-lab-grown-diamonds'
-%}

<div class="pdp__choose"
     data-fye-centre
     data-shape="{{ shape | escape }}"
     data-carat-min="{{ ct_min }}"
     data-carat-max="{{ ct_max }}"
     data-feed-natural="{{ natural_handle }}"
     data-feed-lab="{{ lab_handle }}"
     data-fee-variant="{{ s.centre_fee_variant_id }}"
     data-fee-price="{{ s.centre_fee_price_pennies | default: 0 }}">

  <p class="pdp__label">{{ s.centre_heading | default: 'Centre diamond' }}</p>
  <p class="pdp__choosenote">{{ suitability }}</p>

  <div class="pdp__modes" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ s.centre_heading | default: 'Centre diamond' | escape }}">
    <button type="button"
            class="pdp__mode"
            role="radio"
            aria-checked="false"
            data-fye-centre-mode="required">
      <span class="pdp__radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="pdp__modetitle">{{ s.centre_required_label | default: 'Choose a diamond' }}</span>
      <span class="pdp__modecopy">We supply a matched stone.</span>
    </button>

    <button type="button"
            class="pdp__mode"
            role="radio"
            aria-checked="false"
            data-fye-centre-mode="supplied">
      <span class="pdp__radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="pdp__modetitle">{{ s.centre_supplied_label | default: 'Supply your own' }}</span>
      <span class="pdp__modecopy">We set your {{ shape_lower }} diamond.</span>
      {%- if show_centre_fee_price -%}
        <span class="pdp__modefee">+{{ s.centre_fee_price_pennies | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </button>

    <button type="button"
            class="pdp__mode"
            role="radio"
            aria-checked="false"
            data-fye-centre-mode="none">
      <span class="pdp__radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="pdp__modetitle">{{ s.centre_none_label | default: 'Semi-mount only' }}</span>
      <span class="pdp__modecopy">No centre stone.</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Carries the mode to the cart. Its VALUE is rewritten by fye-ui.js as the
    mode changes; on "required" the field is disabled instead, because the
    chosen stone travels as its own line and a duplicate property on the ring
    line would contradict it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <input type="hidden" name="properties[Centre Diamond]" value="" data-fye-centre-prop disabled>

  {%- comment -%}
    ---- Mode: choose a diamond ----
    Hidden on load like the other two: no mode is selected until the shopper
    picks one.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp__modebody" data-fye-centre-body="required" hidden>
    <p class="pdp__choosenote">
      Add a certified {{ shape_lower }} diamond to complete this ring.
      {{ ct_min }}–{{ ct_max }}ct suits this setting.
    </p>

    <p class="pdp__stonestate" data-fye-stone-state>{{ s.centre_loading | default: 'Checking which diamonds we hold…' }}</p>

    {%- comment -%}
      The chosen stone's summary. Populated by fye-ui.js; empty and hidden
      until a stone is picked, so nothing implies a default choice.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="pdp__stone" data-fye-stone hidden></div>

    <button type="button" class="btn btn--outline pdp__stonebtn" data-fye-picker-open hidden>
      {{ s.centre_picker_label | default: 'Choose your diamond' }}
    </button>

    <p class="pdp__hint fine" data-fye-stone-help hidden>
      Not sure? <a href="{{ s.centre_help_link | default: '/pages/contact-us' }}">We will help you choose</a> — or
      <a href="/collections/{{ natural_handle }}">browse every {{ shape_lower }} diamond</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Mode: supply your own ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp__modebody" data-fye-centre-body="supplied" hidden>
    {%- if s.centre_supplied_note != blank -%}
      <p class="pdp__choosenote">{{ s.centre_supplied_note }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <input type="hidden" name="properties[Setting service]" value="Customer's own centre diamond" data-fye-centre-service disabled>

    {%- comment -%}
      The waiver is a real checkbox with a real label, and add-to-cart is
      blocked until it is ticked — we are setting a stone we have not graded
      and cannot be liable for it. Disabled when this mode is not chosen, so
      an untouched waiver never reaches an order.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <label class="pdp__waiver">
      <input type="checkbox"
             name="properties[Waiver]"
             value="Accepted"
             data-fye-centre-waiver
             disabled>
      <span>{{ s.centre_waiver_text | default: 'I understand that stones supplied by me are set at my own risk, and that For Your Eternity cannot be held liable for damage to a stone we have not graded.' }}</span>
    </label>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    ---- The picker modal ----
    One set of markup at every width: the grid becomes a single column on a
    phone and the filter block becomes a disclosure. Never a second copy of
    the content (conventions §3).

    Rendered inert — no stones, no ranges. fye-ui.js fills the results, sets
    the slider bounds from the stones actually returned, and only then reveals
    the open button. A modal that opens onto "0 stones" is worse than a button
    that has not appeared yet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp__modal" data-fye-picker hidden>
    <div class="pdp__modalscrim" data-fye-picker-close></div>

    <div class="pdp__modalpanel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="pdp-picker-title">
      <div class="pdp__modalhead">
        <div>
          <h2 class="pdp__modaltitle" id="pdp-picker-title">Choose your {{ shape_lower }} diamond</h2>
          <p class="pdp__modalsub">{{ ct_min }}–{{ ct_max }}ct suits this setting. Every stone is supplied with its certificate.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="pdp__modalx" data-fye-picker-close aria-label="Close">
          {%- render 'icon', name: 'close' -%}
        </button>
      </div>

      <details class="pdp__filters" data-fye-picker-filters>
        <summary class="pdp__filterssum">Filters</summary>

        <div class="pdp__filtersbody">
          <div class="pdp__filter">
            <span class="pdp__filterlbl">Carat <span class="pdp__filterval" data-fye-ct-label></span></span>
            <div class="pdp__range" data-fye-range="ct">
              <input type="range" data-fye-range-min aria-label="Minimum carat">
              <input type="range" data-fye-range-max aria-label="Maximum carat">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pdp__filter">
            <span class="pdp__filterlbl">Budget <span class="pdp__filterval" data-fye-price-label></span></span>
            <div class="pdp__range" data-fye-range="price">
              <input type="range" data-fye-range-min aria-label="Minimum price">
              <input type="range" data-fye-range-max aria-label="Maximum price">
            </div>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Natural opens first — Ed, 31/08/2026. These rings are sold mainly
            as natural, and opening on lab-grown prices would misrepresent
            them.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="pdp__filter">
            <span class="pdp__filterlbl">Stone type</span>
            <div class="pdp__seg" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Stone type">
              <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="true" class="is-on" data-fye-stone-type="natural">Natural</button>
              <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-fye-stone-type="lab">Lab-grown</button>
              <button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-fye-stone-type="all">Both</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pdp__filter">
            <span class="pdp__filterlbl">Colour</span>
            <div class="pdp__chips" role="group" aria-label="Colour">
              {%- assign colours = 'D,E,F,G,H,I,J' | split: ',' -%}
              {%- for c in colours -%}
                <button type="button" class="pdp__chip" data-fye-chip="colours" data-val="{{ c }}">{{ c }}</button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pdp__filter">
            <span class="pdp__filterlbl">Clarity</span>
            <div class="pdp__chips" role="group" aria-label="Clarity">
              {%- assign clarities = 'FL,IF,VVS1,VVS2,VS1,VS2' | split: ',' -%}
              {%- for c in clarities -%}
                <button type="button" class="pdp__chip" data-fye-chip="clarities" data-val="{{ c }}">{{ c }}</button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="pdp__filter">
            <span class="pdp__filterlbl">Certificate</span>
            <div class="pdp__chips" role="group" aria-label="Certificate">
              {%- assign certs = 'GIA,IGI' | split: ',' -%}
              {%- for c in certs -%}
                <button type="button" class="pdp__chip" data-fye-chip="certs" data-val="{{ c }}">{{ c }}</button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <div class="pdp__modaltools">
        <p class="pdp__count" data-fye-picker-count aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="pdp__toolsright">
          <label class="pdp__sortlbl" for="pdp-picker-sort">Sort</label>
          <select class="pdp__select pdp__sort" id="pdp-picker-sort" data-fye-picker-sort>
            <option value="price-asc">Price, low to high</option>
            <option value="price-desc">Price, high to low</option>
            <option value="ct-desc">Carat, high to low</option>
            <option value="ct-asc">Carat, low to high</option>
            <option value="colour-asc">Colour, best first</option>
            <option value="clarity-asc">Clarity, best first</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pdp__stones" data-fye-picker-results></div>

      <div class="pdp__modalfoot">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--outline" data-fye-picker-more hidden>Show more stones</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn" data-fye-picker-confirm disabled>Use this diamond</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
